{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/clax/SKILL.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:30:31.539185Z","id":"495f214e507aa3d9b7a795876db88517d130c4c1380943edf9ed4c1eef8e94e5","body":{"detail":"'means your person's rights changed' covers a narrowing and the owner changing the person's rights, but not a creator or the owner removing a raise of this agent (docs/contract.md 'Rights', 'Removing a raise'). The instruction that follows (leave the thread, do not ask) is right in every case. The same sentence is in plugins/clax/skills/clax/SKILL.md:430, plugins/clax-grok/skills/clax/SKILL.md:444 and plugins/pi/skills/clax/SKILL.md:424.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"a1aaba18b8dc69a136456ae53a652e4f74a85b9ed7384fa05e9a15deabeff78e"},"suggested_fix":"'means your rights on that page changed'.","summary":"The skill says a lost-access notice means the agent's person's rights changed; a removed raise or the owner's change does it too","tags":["review","task:24","docs","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
